{
  "id": "listening-post",
  "name": "The listening post",
  "description": "The branch's listening post on Pylon Forty's second ring. The front is a lift-maintenance office nobody uses: a buzzing fluorescent tube, a pegboard of clean tools, a workbench with a lift parts binder, grey coveralls on a rail, and a door with a frosted glass panel out to the stair. Through a half-open steel partition, the real room: a long desk under six monitors of grainy camera feeds of the streets under the Spine, a waveform and a signal map; a headset, an overflowing ashtray, a chipped mug and a green-shaded desk lamp; a tall comms rack of blinking green and amber lights. Floor-to-ceiling shelves of brown file boxes, a filing cabinet with a coffee maker and a scorched pot on it, and a narrow cot with a rumpled blanket in the corner. Bare concrete, pipes and cable trays overhead, no windows at all.",
